{"availability":"available","full":"TavoloPerUno/py-visualize-accelerometry","name":"py-visualize-accelerometry","description":"Web-based tool for visualizing and annotating accelerometry data. Supports collaborative labeling of activity segments in large time-series recordings. Built with Panel and Bokeh. Docs: https://tavoloperuno.github.io/py_visualize_accelerometry/ | Demo: https://tavoloperuno-accelerometry-viewer-demo.hf.space/","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2021-01-07T20:26:07Z","updated":"2026-07-25T17:08:45Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://tavoloperuno.github.io/py-visualize-accelerometry/","topics":["accelerometry","activity-recognition","aging-research","annotation-tool","bokeh","chair-stand-test","clinical-assessment","data-visualization","gait-analysis","hdf5","nshap","panel","physical-activity","physical-performance","python","signal-visualization","time-series","timed-up-and-go","wearable-sensors","wrist-accelerometer"],"demo":"https://tavoloperuno-accelerometry-viewer-demo.hf.space/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:39.896Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:39.896Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:39.896Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:40.833Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:32:39.896Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A web app for viewing and annotating tri-axial accelerometry data. Research teams use it to label activity segments in long recordings together. Built with Panel and Bokeh. Sensor-agnostic: any HDF5 file with timestamp, x, y, z columns works."],"features":["LTTB downsampling. Renders 500K+ points smoothly by reducing each axis to 10,000 visually representative points (Largest Triangle Three Buckets).","Server-side HDF5 filtering. Loads only the visible time window via PyTables where clauses. Under 20 ms on 1 GB+ files.","Fast navigation. Pre